<description>&lt;p&gt;Violence continues in South Sudan with armed attacks by rebel and SPLA-IO forces killing civilians in Tonj East and Warrap State, including women, children and a football referee shot in the head. Intercommunal clashes in Tonj East have prompted UNMISS to support deterrence efforts, while a separate attack in Greater Pibor left three dead and one wounded. MSF suspended all activities in Yei River County after staff were abducted. A rights group demanded justice for survivors of sexual violence, and the UNDP resident representative issued a message of solidarity. There were 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMidkFVX3lxTFBOTF9pY0NmbXA5N0JTUTJpSl9mdEY4aDExN3hPeENmbUVHRW5NVEpERGxidERUbEVCMWE3LUlPRVdiY1hHa0FLUGxiblhMUk9tQkY1aU04bXdtam0wd2dCMHdJazZHLVpsSER6UURucjMtSXlBTkE?oc=5&quot;&gt;Mail &amp;amp; Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiyAFBVV95cUxPMXNMeVJ1MnEwUVJUa0ZIdnpzN05nVnNFYVpmeE0wZ2QzZktQbTR6Vmp4dncwOGpqeEhhTEg4TWoxNXd0TXRCTTQzaE9RVGJEUG1NZkM0VnU5TlZ3TU5aem9wUXF5djZTWGI2WFlmbHozMFVLck9jb3NlNUJmdzMtVkJWVm5sbUFKdTR0bzlDNTh6eU9saWppc2E0UVluS1J2MEFuVFpFZEJLLUZZMkhOeFJsVnZkY0hSVVJnNnJfaHRxeXNLYlN2Vw?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinAFBVV95cUxOY2xHT3c0cmN2YzNOdnAxN0xiLTNmdFVFcHlVQWdPRF95QUI1S21lME1IallCQWNKSHZKWE91alp4NWljVXVpdnhWUWxreW5CdDdtRl9JRERxcTE0Z0tVNTZzNjhFU2FCVk41bkNXazdPaFdkVWQtYkloUmUyX1R3d280eGhZZlRmV2xsVktFc2Vpd2RmT1NpOUN1bUw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Yeni Safak English&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitgFBVV95cUxOOFAycFN2QUd6LXd2ZTlvUDlZdFRIeGhuRnBWWmduNnMzNUVHcVpXWkxrTkVxNFYzbHpRS00zZThPVnZJN20wNmtTcGtKa0stVFByeXdMdTQ0UnNSUURtb